{
  "$comment": "Formats whose embedded metadata the schemas of hamk-uas/stac-schema-explorer describe, and the conventions that add fields to it. Every node of a format document is checked against the format schema and the schemas of the conventions that apply to it. A convention applies when it is declared (in `zarr_conventions` or the global `Conventions` attribute) or, for conventions without a declaration mechanism, when a node has one of its `detection` members (paths into the node). `checked` records when the specification was last checked, its latest release then (`latest`, absent when it has no releases) and where that was seen; `maturity` is the maturity a convention states (the zarr-conventions classification: Proposal, Pilot, Candidate, Stable, Deprecated).",
